4. What is Agentic Loop..?
When you invoke (ask claude code to do something) it uses an agentic loop to perform the requested task.

Your prompt--> Model-->Gather Context-->Take Action-->Verify Results.

While executing the three phases it will perform calls to tools aka tool calls to aid it accomplishing its tasks.

tools are just functions of code that calls to external programs.

You can interrupt the loop at any time to help correct the agent if you think its misguided.

5. Agentic loop - Tool Calls 
Tools are Code functions that an agent is aware of and can invoke to complete their tasks.

Tools often call out to external program and in turn let the agent interact outside its environment and predefined knowledge.

Your prompt-->Gather Context-->Take Action-->Verify Results-->Done.

Gather Context,Take Action,Verify Results are Tool Calls. 

Gather Context->read_file("tests/test_payment.py")

Take Action->edit_file("src/payment.py", change="fix tax calculation")

Verify Results->run_command("pytest")

Examples of different types of tool calls

Gather Context
1. File readers
2. Search APIs
3. Database queries ( are also called as RAG)
4. Codebase Scanners
5. System state queries

Take Action
1. code editing
2. Running commands
3. Writing Files
4. Calling APIs
5. Executing scripts

Verify Results
1. run tests
2. Compile code
3. Query output
4. Inspect logs
5. Compare results

The Claude Code built-in tools fall into five categories:

1. File Operations read files, edit code, create new files, rename and reorganize.
2. Search find searches files by pattern, search content with regex, explore codebases.
3. Execution Run executes shell commands, start servers, run tests, use git.
4. Web Search searches the web, fetch documentation, look up error messages.
5. Code intelligence looks at type errors and warnings after edits, jump to definitions,